WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.426 --> 00:00:04.523
- I've been doing drag for
about three and a half years,

00:00:04.523 --> 00:00:07.161
sounds about right, three or four years.

00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:11.091
At first I started doing it
as just for fun or a little

00:00:11.091 --> 00:00:14.841
hobby of mine, and
somehow it became serious.

00:00:15.894 --> 00:00:18.477
(upbeat music)

00:00:21.173 --> 00:00:23.413
Coming out to my family
wasn't as hard as it is

00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:26.503
to other people cause I
kind of knew they were gonna

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:29.189
accept me but it was just
hard because I didn't want

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:32.132
them to feel like I was a failure.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.863
And my father I haven't
told him to the day

00:00:34.863 --> 00:00:37.547
I haven't told him yet,
but I'm sure he knows

00:00:37.547 --> 00:00:39.822
I feel like sometimes you
don't really have to actually

00:00:39.822 --> 00:00:42.432
tell the person that you're gay.

00:00:42.432 --> 00:00:45.200
It's just something that
they know and they're okay

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.839
with and you could see
it through their actions

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:51.030
or the way they talk to you.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.947
(electronic music)

00:01:18.526 --> 00:01:21.091
I'm first generation
Latino, well my dad is from

00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:24.744
Jalisco, and my mom is from Mexicali.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:28.911
My drag character is more
like dark and mesmerizing.

00:01:29.911 --> 00:01:33.347
And when I'm not doing
that my other side is my

00:01:33.347 --> 00:01:37.597
Latina side where I incorporate
just music that I listen

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:39.827
to also with my outfits I
love to incorporate my culture

00:01:39.827 --> 00:01:44.380
and bring all that in, because
I am proud of my culture,

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.394
I think it's beautiful to be a Latino.

00:01:47.394 --> 00:01:48.811
Drag is just art.

00:01:49.959 --> 00:01:51.574
For me it's just art.

00:01:51.574 --> 00:01:54.128
A way of self expression
cause I still think of myself

00:01:54.128 --> 00:01:54.961
as a man.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:59.147
It doesn't change just
because I'm a drag queen

00:01:59.147 --> 00:02:00.230
or I'm queer.

00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:04.212
(electronic music)

00:02:04.212 --> 00:02:06.462
(applause)

00:02:10.286 --> 00:02:11.939
(calm music)

00:02:11.939 --> 00:02:14.542
Even though in my culture
men are perceived as more

00:02:14.542 --> 00:02:17.437
strong, more confident
beings, it's funny that I get

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.571
in drag because I feel like
a woman is more confident

00:02:20.571 --> 00:02:22.509
and more powerful.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.782
In the Latin communities
the man is the head of the

00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:27.013
household, but the woman is
the one who holds the balls.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.049
(laughing)

00:02:28.049 --> 00:02:30.910
In a way I feel like she's stronger.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.603
I saw that growing up with my mother.

00:02:32.603 --> 00:02:35.686
Like she'll do anything for her kids.

00:02:41.622 --> 00:02:43.276
Hearing stories of my brothers and sisters

00:02:43.276 --> 00:02:46.089
in Latin America and other
countries being attacked

00:02:46.089 --> 00:02:50.511
and raped for being who they
are really makes me think

00:02:50.511 --> 00:02:54.428
how fortunate I am to be
born in United States.

00:02:56.246 --> 00:02:58.603
It makes me think that if my
parents wouldn't have moved

00:02:58.603 --> 00:03:01.539
here, I don't think I'll
be feeling comfortable

00:03:01.539 --> 00:03:04.275
enough to be doing drag or
stepping out of the house

00:03:04.275 --> 00:03:05.442
with a wig on.

00:03:07.252 --> 00:03:09.835
(somber music)

00:03:14.705 --> 00:03:16.646
People here still like look at me and

00:03:16.646 --> 00:03:20.563
take a second look when
they see me walking by.

00:03:21.814 --> 00:03:23.840
The difference is that it
doesn't matter to me here

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.770
cause although something
could happen to me

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.270
I just don't care.

00:03:30.633 --> 00:03:34.012
(somber music)

00:03:34.012 --> 00:03:36.412
And that's why I just feel
like when I hear those

00:03:36.412 --> 00:03:38.973
stories it just makes me not take anything

00:03:38.973 --> 00:03:43.426
for granted and be so thankful
for having been born here.

00:03:43.426 --> 00:03:45.619
And the struggles that my
parents went through to

00:03:45.619 --> 00:03:46.786
get me here.

00:03:46.786 --> 00:03:49.226
And that's why part of me
still wants to incorporate

00:03:49.226 --> 00:03:52.370
my culture in my drag
cause I'm so proud of it

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.681
and it's something that
makes me truly happy

00:03:54.681 --> 00:03:56.584
to put it out there and let everybody know

00:03:56.584 --> 00:04:00.001
that I'm a Latino and I feel unstoppable.

00:04:01.051 --> 00:04:03.634
(somber music)

